From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:08:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Changing clothes: the stage keeps its look while the new
 outfit is fitted, and pointing at a tile starts the fitting.

Picking another outfit fits it to the face in the browser at the stage's size (0.5 s at 512, 0.8 s at 1024 when the
worker is free; longer behind the dialog's own tiles), and the stage stayed empty meanwhile.

- The try-on stage keeps the look it last showed while another outfit is fitted to the same face (a new face still
  clears it, as before).
- AppearanceIdPicker reports a pointer (or focus) resting on a tile for 120 ms (onOptionHover); the clothes and whole
  costume pickers use it to start the stage-size fitting (prepareStageOutfit), so a pointed-at outfit is usually ready
  by the click.

Checked in the local Studio (East Asian woman): clicked straight away 0.54 s with the old look kept, never empty;
pointed at first then clicked 0.03 s; with a plate hairstyle on, the same, and the hair stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
